==English==

===Etymology===
Compound of {{compound|red|neck|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɹɛdnɛk/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|slang|pejorative}} A poor, [[rural]], [[white]] [[Southern United States|Southern]] person (of either gender)<ref>[http://www.hit-country-music-lyrics.com/redneck-woman-lyrics.html Country Music Lyrics New Country Tunes]</ref>; especially, one who is regarded as [[rowdy]], [[arrogant]], [[egotistical]], a [[braggart]], etc.
# {{label|en|slang}} The nickname given to miners who wore red [[bandana]]s for identification during the West Virginia mine war of 1921.<ref>[http://www.wvculture.org/hiStory/minewars.html West Virginia Division of Culture and History]</ref>
# {{label|en|UK|archaic}} The nickname given to [[Roman Catholics]] in the nineteenth and twentieth centuries.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|cracker}}, {{l|en|hick}}, {{l|en|hillbilly}}, {{l|en|peckerwood}}, {{l|en|white trash}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|redneckish}}
* {{l|en|redneckism}}
* {{l|en|rednecky}}

